Chapter: GuardNest

 A MATCH INSIDE A GUARD. `emit-wat-match` parks the scrutinee in ONE per-function
 local, `$_s`, and emits each branch's guard INSIDE the condition -- before the
 else-chain re-reads `$_s` for the branches below. A `when` in a guard reassigns
 it, so once that guard is false every later branch dispatches on the INNER
 scrutinee instead of the outer one.

 `Boxed 5` is the case: its guard runs, the inner `when` overwrites `$_s` with 5,
 the guard is false, and the `is Boxed (y)` arm below then reads a `$_s` that no
 longer holds the Boxed record. The match must be INLINE in the guard: a call to
 a function whose body is a match is compiled as a separate wasm function with a
 `$_s` of its own, and agrees.

 Expected, and what the zig plug prints: 100, 205, 305.

  Box =
    | Boxed (Integer)
    | Plain (Integer)

  classify : Box -> Integer
  classify (v) =
   when v
    is Boxed (x) when (when x is 7 -> True is otherwise -> False) -> 100
    is Boxed (y) -> 200 + y
    is Plain (z) -> 300 + z

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (classify (Boxed 7)))
    print-line-uni (show (classify (Boxed 5)))
    print-line-uni (show (classify (Plain 5)))
  end
